        "evidence_id": "E002",
        "passage_id": "P002",
        "statement_status": "current_disposition",
        "quote": "Ordered that the order is reversed, on the law, with costs, and the motion of the defendant Board of Managers at Vista at Kingsgate, Section II, for summary judgment dismissing the complaint insofar as asserted against it is denied."
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E003",
        "passage_id": "P002",
        "statement_status": "allegation",
        "quote": "The plaintiff allegedly was injured when she slipped and fell twice in succession on two patches of ice on the property of a condominium complex owned by the defendant Board of Managers at Vista at Kingsgate, Section II (hereinafter Vista II). The plaintiff allegedly saw both patches of ice before she stepped on them, but she had to traverse those patches to reach her destinations."
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E004",
        "passage_id": "P002",
        "statement_status": "court_finding",
        "quote": "A property owner will be held liable for a slip-and-fall accident involving snow and ice on its property only when it created the dangerous condition which caused the accident or had actual or constructive notice of its existence"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E005",
        "passage_id": "P003",
        "statement_status": "court_finding",
        "quote": "Here, Vista II failed to establish, prima facie, that it did not have constructive notice of the alleged patches of ice."
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E006",
        "passage_id": "P004",
        "statement_status": "testimony_or_record",
        "quote": "In support of its motion, Vista II submitted, inter alia, the deposition testimony of the managing agent of the property, who merely testified about his general inspection practices and provided no evidence regarding any specific inspection of the areas in question prior to the plaintiff's falls"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E007",
        "passage_id": "P004",
        "statement_status": "court_finding",
        "quote": "The Supreme Court's reliance on Gushin v Whispering Hills Condominium I (96 AD3d 721 [2012]), is misplaced because here, unlike in that case, the conditions were visible and apparent."
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E008",
        "passage_id": "P004",
        "statement_status": "current_disposition",
        "quote": "Accordingly, the Supreme Court should have denied Vista II's motion for summary judgment dismissing the complaint insofar as asserted against it regardless of the sufficiency of the opposition papers"
      }
